                      "type": "text",
                      "name": "t:names.text",
                      "settings": {
                        "text": "<p>I was developing a curved second toe. I had probably broken it as some point. I didn't want to go to a podiatrist because I had previously only been given surgery as possible options for other issues. </p><p>Correct Toes were recommended by several reputable podiatrists and PTs on line. I liked that the recommendation along with Correct Toes was that exercises were necessary for actual recovery and those were provided by the company. </p><p>After following the exercises and wearing the devices for several weeks, I am out of pain. I am even getting relief for my tailor bunion.</p>",
                        "width": "fit-content",
                        "max_width": "normal",
                        "alignment": "left",
